 "reconciliation": "ALL TWENTY-ONE columns the sheet carries a printed total for close exactly, residual zero on every one: nine free-white male, seven free-white female, and four free-coloured. TWO FOOTER READINGS WERE CORRECTED BY THAT CHECK and both are recorded, because a closure that hides its corrections is worth nothing. FIRST, THE ENUMERATOR'S 4 IS TWO PARALLEL STROKES. His footing for males 30 under 40 was read as 16 from a reduced overview; at 6x it is a 1 followed by two near-parallel diagonals, the identical form he uses for the 4 in the males 10-under-15 footing two cells to its left. It is 14, which is what the thirty lines sum to. The ticket that split this work named that glyph in advance — 'a hand whose 4 is two strokes that read as 11' — and this is the sheet that pays for it. SECOND, the females 10-under-15 cell on line 2 was read as a 4 and is a 1: at 9x it is a single bold stroke with a fleck of bleed-through above and left of it, and the column closes at 5 with the 1 and stands at 8 with the 4. No total was adjusted to make a reading come out; in both cases the reading changed and the enumerator's figure stood.",
 "derived_totals": {
  "free_white_males": 97,
  "free_white_females": 54,
  "free_white_persons": 151,
  "free_coloured_persons": 7,
  "persons_total": 158,
  "note": "summed from the read cells. The sheet prints no grand total of its own on this exposure, so these are DERIVED and labelled as such; they are not transcribed data."
 },
 "free_coloured_note": "NOT blank on this leaf, and it is the only sheet of group 26-50 read so far that is not. Seven free-coloured persons are enumerated across three lines: line 3 carries one male 24 under 36, and lines 10 and 11 are households standing ENTIRELY in this block with no free-white cell at all. The four columns involved carry printed footings (1, 3, 1, 2) and all four close against the read cells.",
 "pairing": {
  "paired_to_printed_page": null,
  "state": "unpaired",
  "why": "a left sheet carries its own printed page number (211) and its own names, so it needs no pairing to be read. Its pairing to a CONTINUATION sheet is the separate reading T-0528/T-0539 make, and it is not asserted here.",
  "page_population_key": 158,
  "page_population_key_note": "the persons this sheet enumerates, free white and free coloured together, derived from the read cells and closing against twenty-one printed column totals. A continuation sheet whose TOTAL footing reads 158 is this leaf; that test belongs to the pairing ticket."
 },
